declare
  v_plan constant jsonb := $audit_plan${"generatedBy":"scripts/prod-open/sat-manual-patches-sql.ts","problems":[{"patch_id":"E1019-M001","problem_id":"01d7207e-c5d8-4b93-a2ea-ba5b57b7ff0e","from_version_id":"78d5b304-f76c-4a00-9cc3-43c8bdcd223f","expect":{"passage":"A city planner models the height of a pedestrian bridge arch above a walkway using the function $h(x) = -0.5x^2 + 4x$, where $x$ is the horizontal distance in meters from the base of the arch and $h(x)$ is the height in meters. The graph of $h$ is shown.","explanation":"이차함수 $h(x) = -0.5x^2 + 4x$의 최댓값은 꼭짓점에서 나타난다. 꼭짓점의 x좌표는 $x = -\\frac{b}{2a} = -\\frac{4}{2(-0.5)} = 4$이다. 그래프에서도 곡선이 $x=4$ 부근에서 가장 높은 지점(대칭의 정점)을 이루는 것을 확인할 수 있다. 다른 선택지들은 x절편(0과 8)이나 그 중간이 아닌 임의의 점을 최댓값 위치로 착각한 경우다.","explanation_en":"The maximum of the quadratic function $h(x) = -0.5x^2 + 4x$ occurs at its vertex. The x-coordinate of the vertex is $x = -\\frac{b}{2a} = -\\frac{4}{2(-0.5)} = 4$. The graph also confirms that the curve reaches its highest point (the peak of the symmetry) near $x=4$. The other choices mistake the x-intercepts (0 and 8) or an arbitrary point other than the midpoint for the location of the maximum."},"set":{"passage":"A city planner models the height of a pedestrian bridge arch above a walkway, where $x$ is the horizontal distance in meters from the base of the arch and $h(x)$ is the height in meters. The graph of $h$ is shown.","explanation":"그래프에서 곡선이 가장 높은 점(꼭짓점)에 이르는 곳의 x좌표를 읽는다. 곡선은 x = 0과 x = 8에서 x축과 만나고, 좌우 대칭이므로 정점은 그 가운데인 x = 4에서 나타난다. 따라서 최대 높이가 되는 x는 4이다. 다른 선택지는 x절편(0, 8)이나 정점이 아닌 임의의 점을 최댓값 위치로 착각한 경우다.","explanation_en":"Read the graph for the x-coordinate of the highest point on the curve. The curve meets the x-axis at x = 0 and x = 8 and is symmetric, so its peak lies midway, at x = 4. Therefore the arch reaches its maximum height at x = 4. The other choices mistake the x-intercepts or an arbitrary point for the location of the maximum."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.271Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -1~9, y -2~10), 가로축 x (meters), 세로축 h(x) (meters). h: y = −0.5x² + 4x."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M001","fromVersionId":"78d5b304-f76c-4a00-9cc3-43c8bdcd223f","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M002","problem_id":"079d2fb7-55f3-455f-a32c-32b252e0da59","from_version_id":"340e0200-5521-439a-a0a6-c963b2facbb1","expect":{"passage":"The graph of the exponential function $r(x) = 3 \\cdot 2^x$ and the horizontal line $y = 24$ are shown in the same $xy$-plane.","explanation":"그래프에서 지수함수 $y = r(x)$와 직선 $y = 24$가 만나는 점의 $x$좌표를 찾으면 된다. 그래프를 보면 두 그래프는 $x = 3$에서 교차한다. 대수적으로 확인하면 $3 \\cdot 2^x = 24$이므로 $2^x = 8 = 2^3$, 따라서 $x = 3$이다. 따라서 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"We need the $x$-coordinate of the point where the exponential function $y = r(x)$ meets the line $y = 24$. In the graph, the two curves intersect at $x = 3$. Checking algebraically, $3 \\cdot 2^x = 24$ gives $2^x = 8 = 2^3$, so $x = 3$. Therefore the answer is B."},"set":{"passage":"The graph of an exponential function $r$ and the horizontal line $y = 24$ are shown in the same $xy$-plane.","explanation":"그래프에서 곡선 $y = r(x)$와 직선 $y = 24$가 만나는 점의 $x$좌표를 읽는다. 두 그래프는 $x = 3$에서 교차하므로 $r(x) = 24$를 만족하는 값은 $x = 3$이다. 따라서 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"Read the $x$-coordinate of the point where the curve $y = r(x)$ meets the line $y = 24$. The two graphs intersect at $x = 3$, so $r(x) = 24$ when $x = 3$. Therefore the answer is B."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.275Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -2~5, y 0~30). r: y = 3·2^x; 직선 y = 24: y = 24."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M002","fromVersionId":"340e0200-5521-439a-a0a6-c963b2facbb1","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M003","problem_id":"0b94e63d-1d30-4fdb-ad23-2ea8895e0978","from_version_id":"40cdedc9-ee3d-449c-a70f-a7acb7022511","expect":{"passage":"The function $f(x) = -2(x - 3)^2 + 8$ models the height, in feet, of a water arc from a decorative fountain jet, where $x$ is the horizontal distance, in feet, from the jet's base. The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown.","explanation":"$f(x) = -2(x-3)^2 + 8$ 은 꼭짓점이 $(3, 8)$인 아래로 볼록(사실 위로 볼록, 최댓값)인 포물선이다. 포물선은 꼭짓점을 지나는 수직선 $x=3$에 대해 대칭이므로, $x=1$에서의 높이와 같은 높이를 갖는 다른 x값은 꼭짓점을 기준으로 대칭인 점이다. $x=1$은 꼭짓점 $x=3$보다 2만큼 작으므로, 대칭점은 $x=3+2=5$이다. 확인: $f(1) = -2(1-3)^2+8 = -2(4)+8=0$, $f(5)=-2(5-3)^2+8=-2(4)+8=0$. 두 값이 같으므로 $x=5$가 답이다.","explanation_en":"$f(x) = -2(x-3)^2 + 8$ is a parabola with vertex $(3, 8)$ that opens downward (it has a maximum). A parabola is symmetric about the vertical line through its vertex, $x=3$, so the other $x$-value with the same height as $x=1$ is the point symmetric about the vertex. Since $x=1$ is 2 less than the vertex's $x=3$, the symmetric point is $x=3+2=5$. Check: $f(1) = -2(1-3)^2+8 = -2(4)+8=0$ and $f(5)=-2(5-3)^2+8=-2(4)+8=0$. The two values are equal, so the answer is $x=5$."},"set":{"passage":"The function $f$ models the height, in feet, of a water arc from a decorative fountain jet, where $x$ is the horizontal distance, in feet, from the jet's base. The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown.","explanation":"그래프에서 $x = 1$일 때의 높이는 0이다(곡선이 x축 위의 점 $(1, 0)$을 지난다). 같은 높이 0을 갖는 다른 점을 찾으면 곡선이 x축과 다시 만나는 $x = 5$이다. 포물선은 꼭짓점의 수직선 $x = 3$에 대해 대칭이므로 $x = 1$의 대칭점이 $x = 5$이다. 따라서 답은 $x = 5$이다.","explanation_en":"On the graph, the height at $x = 1$ is 0 (the curve passes through the point $(1, 0)$). The other point on the curve at the same height 0 is where the curve meets the x-axis again, at $x = 5$. The parabola is symmetric about the vertical line through its vertex, $x = 3$, so the mirror image of $x = 1$ is $x = 5$. The answer is $x = 5$."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.277Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -1~7, y -2~10), 가로축 Horizontal distance (feet), 세로축 Height (feet). f: y = −2x² + 12x − 10."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M003","fromVersionId":"40cdedc9-ee3d-449c-a70f-a7acb7022511","fromVersionNo":2}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M004","problem_id":"1473eff6-7ef8-48a6-add7-d241754fdec6","from_version_id":"38f78fff-5fc5-425b-aa46-9fdee6c50071","expect":{"passage":"A graphic designer creates a parabolic arch logo. The function $f(x) = -x^2 + 8x - 7$ models the height (in inches) of the arch above the baseline, where $x$ is the horizontal distance (in inches) from the left edge of the logo. The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown in the xy-plane.","explanation":"그래프에서 높이가 0이 되는 지점은 x절편이다. $f(x) = -x^2+8x-7 = -(x^2-8x+7) = -(x-1)(x-7)$ 이므로 $f(x)=0$ 이 되는 값은 $x=1$과 $x=7$이다. 그래프를 보면 포물선이 아래로 볼록(위로 오목이 아니라 아래로 오목, 즉 최고점을 가진 형태)이고 x축과 두 번 교차하는 지점이 각각 1과 7 근처임을 확인할 수 있다. 따라서 정답은 D번이다.","explanation_en":"The point where the arch's height is 0 is an x-intercept. Since $f(x) = -x^2+8x-7 = -(x^2-8x+7) = -(x-1)(x-7)$, the values where $f(x)=0$ are $x=1$ and $x=7$. In the graph, you can see that the parabola opens downward (concave down, with a maximum point) and crosses the x-axis twice, near 1 and 7. So the answer is D."},"set":{"passage":"A graphic designer creates a parabolic arch logo. The function $f$ models the height (in inches) of the arch above the baseline, where $x$ is the horizontal distance (in inches) from the left edge of the logo. The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown in the xy-plane.","explanation":"높이가 0이 되는 지점은 그래프가 x축과 만나는 x절편이다. 그래프를 보면 포물선이 x축과 $x = 1$과 $x = 7$에서 만난다. 따라서 높이가 0이 되는 두 값은 $x = 1$과 $x = 7$이고, 정답은 D번이다.","explanation_en":"The arch's height is 0 where the graph meets the x-axis, at the x-intercepts. On the graph, the parabola crosses the x-axis at $x = 1$ and $x = 7$. So the two values of $x$ where the height is 0 are $x = 1$ and $x = 7$, and the answer is D."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.280Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -2~10, y -10~12), 가로축 Distance (inches), 세로축 Height (inches). f: y = −x² + 8x − 7."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M004","fromVersionId":"38f78fff-5fc5-425b-aa46-9fdee6c50071","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M005","problem_id":"2c4d3a89-40e8-4de9-9d80-7d91657c2674","from_version_id":"c230feb0-5c39-4c1d-b8cc-1001fc1f84db","expect":{"passage":"An astronomer tracks the altitude of a small asteroid above the horizon, in degrees, as a function of time after it rises. The altitude is modeled by $h(t) = -t^2 + 8t$, where $t$ is measured in hours. The graph of $y = h(t)$, including the point where the asteroid's altitude equals $12$ degrees, is shown below.","explanation":"그래프에서 직선 $y=12$가 곡선 $y=h(t)$와 만나는 두 교점이 P(2, 12)와 Q(6, 12)로 표시되어 있으므로, 고도가 12도가 되는 시각은 $t=2$와 $t=6$이다. 대수적으로 확인하면 $-t^2+8t=12$에서 $t^2-8t+12=0$이므로 $(t-2)(t-6)=0$, 즉 $t=2, 6$이 된다. 따라서 정답은 D번이다.","explanation_en":"In the graph, the two points where the line $y=12$ meets the curve $y=h(t)$ are marked P(2, 12) and Q(6, 12), so the altitude is 12 degrees at $t=2$ and $t=6$. To check algebraically, $-t^2+8t=12$ gives $t^2-8t+12=0$, so $(t-2)(t-6)=0$, that is, $t=2, 6$. So the answer is D."},"set":{"passage":"An astronomer tracks the altitude of a small asteroid above the horizon, in degrees, as a function $h$ of time $t$, in hours, after it rises. The graph of $y = h(t)$, including the point where the asteroid's altitude equals $12$ degrees, is shown below.","explanation":"그래프에서 직선 $y = 12$가 곡선 $y = h(t)$와 만나는 두 교점이 P(2, 12)와 Q(6, 12)로 표시되어 있으므로, 고도가 12도가 되는 시각은 $t = 2$와 $t = 6$이다. 따라서 정답은 D번이다.","explanation_en":"On the graph, the line $y = 12$ meets the curve $y = h(t)$ at the two marked points P(2, 12) and Q(6, 12), so the altitude is 12 degrees at $t = 2$ and $t = 6$. So the answer is D."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.282Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x 0~8, y 0~18), 가로축 Time (hours), 세로축 Altitude (degrees). h: y = −x² + 8x; 직선 y = 12: y = 12; 점 P (2, 12); 점 Q (6, 12)."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M005","fromVersionId":"c230feb0-5c39-4c1d-b8cc-1001fc1f84db","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M006","problem_id":"c93ba362-8516-4e33-b085-ce1b5615787d","from_version_id":"7b28c320-4ffa-4f5e-8f79-8642177a9cb8","expect":{"passage":"A biologist models the population of a bacterial colony, in thousands, $t$ hours after an experiment begins, using the function $P(t) = 2(3)^t$, shown in the graph below.","explanation":"지수함수 $P(t) = 2(3)^t$에서 초기값은 $t=0$일 때의 값이다. $P(0) = 2(3)^0 = 2(1) = 2$이므로 초기 개체 수는 2천 마리이다. 그래프에서도 곡선이 $t=0$일 때 $y$축과 만나는 점의 높이가 2임을 확인할 수 있다. 지수함수 $a \\cdot b^t$ 형태에서 $a$는 항상 $y$절편(초기값)을 나타낸다. 따라서 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"For the exponential function $P(t) = 2(3)^t$, the initial value is the value at $t=0$. Since $P(0) = 2(3)^0 = 2(1) = 2$, the initial population is 2 thousand. The graph also confirms this: the curve meets the $y$-axis at a height of 2 when $t=0$. In the form $a \\cdot b^t$, $a$ always represents the $y$-intercept (the initial value). Therefore, the answer is B."},"set":{"passage":"A biologist models the population of a bacterial colony, in thousands, $t$ hours after an experiment begins. The graph of the population function $P$ is shown below.","explanation":"초기 개체 수는 $t = 0$일 때의 값이다. 그래프에서 곡선이 $t = 0$일 때 $y$축과 만나는 점의 높이를 읽으면 2이다. 따라서 $P(0) = 2$, 즉 초기 개체 수는 2천 마리이고 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"The initial population is the value at $t = 0$. On the graph, the curve meets the $y$-axis at a height of 2 when $t = 0$. So $P(0) = 2$, meaning the initial population is 2 thousand, and the answer is B."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.285Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -1~3, y 0~20), 가로축 Time (hours), 세로축 Population (thousands). P: y = 2·3^x."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M006","fromVersionId":"7b28c320-4ffa-4f5e-8f79-8642177a9cb8","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M007","problem_id":"dcea79ab-0a4c-4923-8c01-21b87e30d90d","from_version_id":"3c7dabf8-6927-4cd9-b3f7-d3972af93f37","expect":{"passage":"An architectural historian studies the profile of a parabolic archway in a 19th-century train station. The function $h(x) = -\\frac{1}{4}x^2 + 3x$ models the height, in feet, of the underside of the arch at a horizontal distance $x$ feet from one base of the arch, where the graph of $h$ is shown.","explanation":"그래프에서 아치의 밑변에 해당하는 두 점 A(0,0)와 B(12,0)가 x절편으로 표시되어 있다. 이는 $h(x) = -\\frac{1}{4}x^2 + 3x = -\\frac{1}{4}x(x-12) = 0$을 풀어도 확인되며, x=0 또는 x=12에서 높이가 0이 된다. 아치의 밑변 너비는 두 x절편 사이의 거리이므로 $12 - 0 = 12$피트이다. 정답은 C번이다.","explanation_en":"On the graph, points A(0,0) and B(12,0), which correspond to the base of the arch, are marked as the x-intercepts. This is also confirmed by solving $h(x) = -\\frac{1}{4}x^2 + 3x = -\\frac{1}{4}x(x-12) = 0$, where the height is 0 at x=0 or x=12. The width of the arch at its base is the distance between the two x-intercepts, which is $12 - 0 = 12$ feet. The answer is C."},"set":{"passage":"An architectural historian studies the profile of a parabolic archway in a 19th-century train station. The function $h$ models the height, in feet, of the underside of the arch at a horizontal distance $x$ feet from one base of the arch, where the graph of $h$ is shown.","explanation":"그래프에서 아치의 밑변에 해당하는 두 점 A(0, 0)와 B(12, 0)가 x절편으로 표시되어 있다. 아치의 밑변 너비는 두 x절편 사이의 거리이므로 $12 - 0 = 12$피트이다. 정답은 C번이다.","explanation_en":"On the graph, points A(0, 0) and B(12, 0), which correspond to the base of the arch, are marked as the x-intercepts. The width of the arch at its base is the distance between the two x-intercepts, which is $12 - 0 = 12$ feet. The answer is C."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.288Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -2~14, y -2~10), 가로축 Horizontal distance (feet), 세로축 Height (feet). h: y = −0.25x² + 3x; 점 A (0, 0); 점 B (12, 0)."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M007","fromVersionId":"3c7dabf8-6927-4cd9-b3f7-d3972af93f37","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M008","problem_id":"eaac2a72-9970-466d-b509-1c34b9b80a26","from_version_id":"fcbdf235-11b3-4f95-a8e1-9da30dcac1ce","expect":{"passage":"The graphs of $y = x^2 - 1$ and $y = 3$ are shown in the same coordinate plane.","explanation":"두 그래프의 교점은 $x^2-1=3$을 만족하는 x값이다. 정리하면 $x^2=4$이므로 $x=2$ 또는 $x=-2$이다. 그래프에서도 대칭적으로 두 점이 원점을 기준으로 좌우에 있는 것을 볼 수 있다. 두 x좌표의 합은 $2+(-2)=0$이다.","explanation_en":"The intersection points of the two graphs are the x-values that satisfy $x^2-1=3$. Simplifying gives $x^2=4$, so $x=2$ or $x=-2$. The graph also shows the two points placed symmetrically on the left and right of the origin. The sum of the two x-coordinates is $2+(-2)=0$."},"set":{"passage":"The graphs of a quadratic function $f$ and the horizontal line $y = 3$ are shown in the same coordinate plane.","explanation":"그래프에서 포물선과 직선 $y = 3$이 만나는 두 점의 x좌표를 읽으면 $x = -2$와 $x = 2$이다. 두 점은 원점을 기준으로 좌우 대칭이므로 x좌표의 합은 $-2 + 2 = 0$이다.","explanation_en":"On the graph, the parabola and the line $y = 3$ meet at the points with $x$-coordinates $-2$ and $2$. The two points are symmetric about the $y$-axis, so the sum of the $x$-coordinates is $-2 + 2 = 0$."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.290Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x -4~4, y -2~6). f: y = x² − 1; 직선 y = 3: y = 3."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M008","fromVersionId":"fcbdf235-11b3-4f95-a8e1-9da30dcac1ce","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M009","problem_id":"58c8d686-47e7-4ce7-95fe-ebfda36d4e60","from_version_id":"01a885fa-75cb-4c49-8fe7-a491e8388ebf","expect":{"passage":"A biologist studying the spread of an invasive plant species models the number of plants, $N(t)$, in a field $t$ years after the species was first observed with the function $N(t) = 40(1.5)^t$. The graph of $y = N(t)$ is shown for $0 \\le t \\le 5$.","explanation":"$N(t) = 40(1.5)^t$에서 300을 넘는 첫 정수 t를 찾는다. $N(4) = 40(1.5)^4 = 40(5.0625) = 202.5$이고, $N(5) = 40(1.5)^5 = 40(7.59375) = 303.75$이다. 따라서 $t=4$일 때는 아직 300을 넘지 않고, $t=5$일 때 처음으로 300을 초과한다. 그래프에서도 곡선이 $y=300$ 선을 $t=5$ 근처에서 넘어서는 것을 확인할 수 있다. 따라서 답은 $t=5$이다.","explanation_en":"From $N(t) = 40(1.5)^t$, find the first integer t for which N exceeds 300. $N(4) = 40(1.5)^4 = 40(5.0625) = 202.5$, and $N(5) = 40(1.5)^5 = 40(7.59375) = 303.75$. So at $t=4$ the value has not yet exceeded 300, and at $t=5$ it first exceeds 300. The graph also confirms that the curve crosses the line $y=300$ near $t=5$. So the answer is $t=5$."},"set":{"passage":"A biologist studying the spread of an invasive plant species models the number of plants, $N(t)$, in a field $t$ years after the species was first observed. The graph of $y = N(t)$ is shown for $0 \\le t \\le 5$.","explanation":"그래프에서 곡선이 $y = 300$ 높이를 넘어서는 지점의 $t$값을 읽는다. $t = 4$일 때 곡선은 아직 300보다 한참 아래(약 200)에 있고, $t = 5$ 근처에서 300에 도달한다. 가장 가까운 정수는 $t = 5$이다.","explanation_en":"Read the $t$-value on the graph where the curve rises above the height $y = 300$. At $t = 4$ the curve is still well below 300 (about 200), and it reaches 300 near $t = 5$. The nearest whole number is $t = 5$."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.291Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x 0~5, y 0~350), 가로축 Time (years), 세로축 Number of plants. N: y = 40·1.5^x."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M009","fromVersionId":"01a885fa-75cb-4c49-8fe7-a491e8388ebf","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M010","problem_id":"2d39235f-33fc-44e9-9945-777c44395d5a","from_version_id":"a60926e9-e94e-4b4c-b147-a1f7c64105e6","expect":{"passage":"A rectangular garden has a length that is $3$ meters more than its width $w$. The area of the garden, in square meters, is modeled by the function $A(w) = w^2 + 3w$. The graph of $y = A(w)$ is shown for $w \\ge 0$.","explanation":"그래프에서 $y=40$일 때의 w값을 읽으면 $w=5$ 부근에서 곡선이 지나감을 알 수 있다. 대수적으로 확인하면 $w^2+3w=40$이므로 $w^2+3w-40=0$, 즉 $(w+8)(w-5)=0$이 되어 $w=5$ 또는 $w=-8$이다. 너비는 음수가 될 수 없으므로 $w=5$이다.","explanation_en":"Reading the graph at $y=40$, the curve passes near $w=5$. To check algebraically, $w^2+3w=40$ gives $w^2+3w-40=0$, so $(w+8)(w-5)=0$ and $w=5$ or $w=-8$. A width cannot be negative, so $w=5$."},"set":{"passage":"A rectangular garden has a length that is $3$ meters more than its width $w$. The area $A$ of the garden, in square meters, is a function of $w$. The graph of $y = A(w)$ is shown for $w \\ge 0$.","explanation":"그래프에서 $y = 40$ (넓이 40 제곱미터)일 때의 $w$값을 읽으면 곡선이 점 $(5, 40)$을 지난다. 따라서 넓이가 40 제곱미터가 되는 너비는 $w = 5$이다.","explanation_en":"On the graph, find the $w$-value where $y = 40$ (an area of 40 square meters). The curve passes through the point $(5, 40)$. So the width that gives an area of 40 square meters is $w = 5$."},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.292Z","issues":[],"alt":"좌표평면(x 0~10, y 0~100), 가로축 Width, w (meters), 세로축 Area (square meters). A: y = x² + 3x."},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M010","fromVersionId":"a60926e9-e94e-4b4c-b147-a1f7c64105e6","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M011","problem_id":"3cdc0ad5-a948-4e18-9906-a91e90334fdb","from_version_id":"fe49203e-f7c8-4f44-8a5b-be6a6d16b5e2","expect":{"passage":"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of the function $f(x) = x^2 - 4x - 5$ intersects the line $y = k$, where $k$ is a constant, at exactly one point. The graph of $f$ is shown.","figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":8,"min":-4,"step":1,"title":"x"},"y":{"max":12,"min":-10,"step":2,"title":"y"}},"objects":[{"fn":"quadratic","id":"f","kind":"function","label":"f","params":[1,-4,-5]}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"passage":"In the $xy$-plane, the graph of the function $f(x) = x^2 - 4x - 5$ intersects the line $y = k$, where $k$ is a constant, at exactly one point.","figure":null,"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.297Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M011","fromVersionId":"fe49203e-f7c8-4f44-8a5b-be6a6d16b5e2","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M012","problem_id":"4cc47e7c-e766-47d8-aa9b-ae16aeb96d71","from_version_id":"aba6ad73-82bb-4792-a396-79ea26f18f33","expect":{"figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":8,"min":0,"step":1,"title":"Time (hours)"},"y":{"max":220,"min":0,"step":20,"title":"Cost (dollars)"}},"objects":[{"domain":[0,8],"fn":"linear","id":"f","kind":"function","label":"C = 25h + 45","params":[25,45]}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"figure":null,"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.297Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M012","fromVersionId":"aba6ad73-82bb-4792-a396-79ea26f18f33","fromVersionNo":3}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M013","problem_id":"e90ca1b1-6000-4e2d-9346-c6f757d5bed7","from_version_id":"54097df7-5ae6-49a8-8b49-870ee0237835","expect":{"passage":"An economic historian is studying the relationship between two competing currencies' exchange indices during a period of monetary reform. The index value $y$ of Currency 1 as a function of months since the reform began, $x$, satisfies $$y = -3x + 24$$ and the index value of Currency 2 satisfies $$y = x + 4$$ The graphs of both equations are shown, intersecting at point $Q$.","question":"What is the $x$-coordinate of point $Q$, the intersection of the two lines shown?","figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":10,"min":0,"step":1,"title":"Months since reform began"},"y":{"max":30,"min":0,"step":3,"title":"Exchange index value"}},"objects":[{"id":"c1","intercept":24,"kind":"line","label":"Currency 1","slope":-3},{"id":"c2","intercept":4,"kind":"line","label":"Currency 2","slope":1},{"id":"Q","kind":"intersection","label":"Q","of":["c1","c2"]}],"type":"plane"},"explanation":"두 식 $y = -3x + 24$와 $y = x + 4$를 연립하면 $-3x + 24 = x + 4$가 된다. 양변에 $3x$를 더하면 $24 = 4x + 4$, 양변에서 4를 빼면 $20 = 4x$, 따라서 $x = 5$이다. 이 값을 확인하면 $y = 5 + 4 = 9$로 두 식 모두에서 일치한다. 그래프에서 점 Q도 이 위치에서 두 직선이 교차함을 보여주므로 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"Setting the two equations $y = -3x + 24$ and $y = x + 4$ equal gives $-3x + 24 = x + 4$. Adding $3x$ to both sides gives $24 = 4x + 4$, and subtracting 4 from both sides gives $20 = 4x$, so $x = 5$. Checking this value, $y = 5 + 4 = 9$ in both equations, so they agree. The graph also shows the two lines crossing at point Q at this location, so the answer is B."},"set":{"passage":"An economic historian is studying the relationship between two competing currencies' exchange indices during a period of monetary reform. The index value $y$ of Currency 1 as a function of months since the reform began, $x$, satisfies $$y = -3x + 24$$ and the index value of Currency 2 satisfies $$y = x + 4$$ The two lines intersect at point $Q$.","question":"What is the $x$-coordinate of point $Q$, the intersection of the two lines?","figure":null,"explanation":"두 식 $y = -3x + 24$와 $y = x + 4$를 연립하면 $-3x + 24 = x + 4$가 된다. 양변에 $3x$를 더하면 $24 = 4x + 4$, 양변에서 4를 빼면 $20 = 4x$, 따라서 $x = 5$이다. 이 값을 확인하면 $y = 5 + 4 = 9$로 두 식 모두에서 일치한다. 따라서 점 Q의 x좌표는 5이고 정답은 B번이다.","explanation_en":"Setting the two equations $y = -3x + 24$ and $y = x + 4$ equal gives $-3x + 24 = x + 4$. Adding $3x$ to both sides gives $24 = 4x + 4$, and subtracting 4 from both sides gives $20 = 4x$, so $x = 5$. Checking this value, $y = 5 + 4 = 9$ in both equations, so they agree. So the x-coordinate of point Q is 5, and the answer is B.","figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.298Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M013","fromVersionId":"54097df7-5ae6-49a8-8b49-870ee0237835","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M014","problem_id":"9977438d-6d27-48ed-aebb-c4ad8e08c6c0","from_version_id":"af1907f7-c7e6-445b-aecb-b3947e37410f","expect":{"passage":"An astronomer is comparing the brightness (in relative magnitude units) of two variable stars over time. The brightness of Star X over the observed period is modeled by the equation $$2y - 4x = 6$$ and the brightness of Star Y is modeled by the equation $$y + 2x = 13$$ where $x$ is time in days and $y$ is brightness. The graphs of both equations are shown.","question":"What is the value of $y$ in the solution to the system of equations shown?","figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":8,"min":-1,"step":1,"title":"Time (days)"},"y":{"max":16,"min":-1,"step":2,"title":"Brightness"}},"objects":[{"id":"l1","intercept":3,"kind":"line","label":"Star X","slope":2},{"id":"l2","intercept":13,"kind":"line","label":"Star Y","slope":-2}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"passage":"An astronomer is comparing the brightness (in relative magnitude units) of two variable stars over time. The brightness of Star X over the observed period is modeled by the equation $$2y - 4x = 6$$ and the brightness of Star Y is modeled by the equation $$y + 2x = 13$$ where $x$ is time in days and $y$ is brightness.","question":"What is the value of $y$ in the solution to the system of equations?","figure":null,"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.300Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M014","fromVersionId":"af1907f7-c7e6-445b-aecb-b3947e37410f","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M015","problem_id":"e1f8fcfb-fbe0-45e7-819a-a38851a50e39","from_version_id":"6c7a5e80-bad9-4440-a697-7691f27e43b7","expect":{"figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":8,"min":-6,"step":1,"title":"x"},"y":{"max":8,"min":-6,"step":1,"title":"y"}},"objects":[{"id":"l1","intercept":-1,"kind":"line","label":"ℓ","slope":2},{"id":"l2","intercept":5,"kind":"line","label":"m","slope":-1}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"figure":null,"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.302Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M015","fromVersionId":"6c7a5e80-bad9-4440-a697-7691f27e43b7","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M016","problem_id":"f59b7f57-b596-4235-9902-d8036d9040ff","from_version_id":"35ba1e3b-847b-4fd0-81d1-84be51f51d15","expect":{"figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":35,"min":-2,"step":5,"title":"Tomato seedlings (x)"},"y":{"max":40,"min":-2,"step":5,"title":"Pepper seedlings (y)"}},"objects":[{"id":"l1","intercept":40,"kind":"line","label":"6x + 3y = 120","slope":-2},{"id":"l2","intercept":30,"kind":"line","label":"x + y = 30","slope":-1}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"figure":null,"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.303Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M016","fromVersionId":"35ba1e3b-847b-4fd0-81d1-84be51f51d15","fromVersionNo":1}},{"patch_id":"E1019-M017","problem_id":"d1e251f0-cebc-4187-b79c-37da71685423","from_version_id":"087c1c2c-ceb6-4207-9e2d-bfa4f88d8ccc","expect":{"figure":{"axes":{"x":{"max":10,"min":-6,"step":1},"y":{"max":8,"min":-6,"step":1}},"objects":[{"at":[4,2],"id":"P","kind":"point","label":"(4, 2)"},{"id":"l1","intercept":4,"kind":"line","label":"y = -1/2 x + 4","slope":-0.5},{"id":"l2","intercept":-2,"kind":"line","label":"other line","slope":1}],"type":"plane"}},"set":{"figure":null,"figure_checked":false},"render_check":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T02:08:26.305Z","issues":[]},"audit_fix":{"source":"external_audit_2026-10-13","patch":"E1019-M017","fromVersionId":"087c1c2c-ceb6-4207-9e2d-bfa4f88d8ccc","fromVersionNo":1}}],"sets":[]}$audit_plan$::jsonb;
  v_actor uuid := (select id from profiles where role = 'admin' order by created_at limit 1);
  u jsonb; s jsonb; a jsonb;
  v_prob problems%rowtype; v_cur problem_versions%rowtype; v_have jsonb; v_want jsonb; v_new uuid;
  v_src mock_exam_sets%rowtype; v_new_set uuid; v_cols text; v_cols_i text; v_pids uuid[];
  v_n int; v_stale int; v_bad text; v_done_p int := 0; v_skip_p int := 0; v_done_s int := 0; v_skip_s int := 0;
begin
  if v_actor is null then raise exception 'No admin profile found.'; end if;

  -- Phase 1: problems -> new published problem version each (same flow as the admin problem editor)
  for u in select * from jsonb_array_elements(v_plan->'problems') loop
    select * into v_prob from problems where id = (u->>'problem_id')::uuid;
    if v_prob.id is null then raise exception '[%] problem % not found', u->>'patch_id', u->>'problem_id'; end if;
    select * into v_cur from problem_versions where id = v_prob.published_version_id;
    if v_cur.id is null then raise exception '[%] problem % has no published version', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id; end if;
    -- final field values = current published version, overridden by the planned new values
    a := jsonb_build_object('passage', v_cur.passage, 'question', v_cur.question, 'options', v_cur.options, 'correct_index', v_cur.correct_index, 'answers', v_cur.answers,
                            'explanation', v_cur.explanation, 'explanation_en', v_cur.explanation_en, 'figure', v_cur.figure, 'statements', v_cur.statements, 'difficulty', v_cur.difficulty,
                            'figure_checked', coalesce(v_cur.figure_checked, false), 'evidence_target', v_cur.evidence_target, 'evidence_span', v_cur.evidence_span,
                            'answer_rationale', v_cur.answer_rationale, 'distractor_error_types', v_cur.distractor_error_types);
    v_have := (select coalesce(jsonb_object_agg(k, a->k), '{}'::jsonb) from jsonb_object_keys(u->'expect') k);
    v_want := (select coalesce(jsonb_object_agg(k, (a || (u->'set'))->k), '{}'::jsonb) from jsonb_object_keys(u->'expect') k);
    if v_have = v_want then v_skip_p := v_skip_p + 1; raise notice '[%] already applied, skipped', u->>'patch_id'; continue; end if;
    if v_have <> u->'expect' then raise exception '[%] DRIFT: the published version of problem % no longer matches the expected old content (re-run the dry-run)', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id; end if;
    a := a || (u->'set');
    if exists (select 1 from problem_versions where problem_id = v_prob.id and status in ('draft', 'in_review')) then
      raise exception '[%] problem % has an open draft/in_review version', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id;
    end if;
    v_new := public.save_problem_draft_version(
      p_problem_id => v_prob.id, p_passage => a->>'passage', p_options => nullif(a->'options', 'null'::jsonb), p_correct_index => (a->>'correct_index')::int,
      p_explanation => a->>'explanation', p_difficulty => a->>'difficulty', p_actor_id => v_actor, p_answers => nullif(a->'answers', 'null'::jsonb),
      p_figure => nullif(a->'figure', 'null'::jsonb), p_figure_checked => coalesce((a->>'figure_checked')::boolean, false), p_statements => nullif(a->'statements', 'null'::jsonb),
      p_question => a->>'question', p_repair_status => null, p_explanation_en => a->>'explanation_en', p_evidence_target => a->>'evidence_target',
      p_evidence_span => a->>'evidence_span', p_answer_rationale => a->>'answer_rationale', p_distractor_error_types => nullif(a->'distractor_error_types', 'null'::jsonb));
    perform public.set_problem_render_check(v_new, u->'render_check');
    perform public.set_problem_quality(v_new, coalesce(v_cur.quality, '{}'::jsonb) || jsonb_build_object('auditFix', u->'audit_fix'));
    perform public.confirm_and_publish_problem_version(v_new, v_actor);
    if u ? 'ap' then perform public.ap_attach_new_version(u->'ap'->>'candidate_key', (u->'ap'->>'item_index')::int, v_new, v_actor); end if;
    v_done_p := v_done_p + 1;
    raise notice '[%] problem % -> new version %', u->>'patch_id', v_prob.id, v_new;
  end loop;

  -- Phase 2: sets -> new set version per affected published set (items of the patched problems point to the new problem versions; snapshots of the rest are copied)
  for s in select * from jsonb_array_elements(v_plan->'sets') loop
    select array_agg(x::uuid) into v_pids from jsonb_array_elements_text(s->'problem_ids') x;
    select * into v_src from mock_exam_sets where set_group_id = (s->>'set_group_id')::uuid and status = 'published' and archived_at is null order by version_no desc limit 1 for update;
    if v_src.id is null then raise exception 'Set group % has no published version (%).', s->>'set_group_id', s->>'name'; end if;
    select count(*) into v_n from mock_exam_set_items i where i.exam_set_id = v_src.id and i.problem_id = any (v_pids);
    if v_n <> cardinality(v_pids) then raise exception 'Set % v% holds % of % target problems.', v_src.name, v_src.version_no, v_n, cardinality(v_pids); end if;
    select count(*) into v_stale from mock_exam_set_items i join problems p on p.id = i.problem_id
     where i.exam_set_id = v_src.id and i.problem_id = any (v_pids) and p.published_version_id is distinct from i.problem_version_id;
    if v_stale = 0 then v_skip_s := v_skip_s + 1; raise notice 'set % v% already up to date, skipped', v_src.name, v_src.version_no; continue; end if;
    perform pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtextextended('mock_exam_new_version:' || v_src.set_group_id::text, 0));
    if exists (select 1 from mock_exam_sets where set_group_id = v_src.set_group_id and status = 'draft') then
      raise exception 'A draft version already exists for set % - publish or archive it first.', v_src.name;
    end if;
    v_new_set := gen_random_uuid();
    select string_agg(quote_ident(column_name), ', ' order by ordinal_position) into v_cols
      from information_schema.columns where table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'mock_exam_sets' and is_generated = 'NEVER'
       and column_name not in ('id', 'version_no', 'status', 'created_by', 'created_at', 'published_at', 'published_by', 'archived_at', 'access_tier');
    execute format('insert into mock_exam_sets (id, version_no, status, created_by, access_tier, %s) select $1, $2, ''draft'', $3, ''tutoring'', %s from mock_exam_sets where id = $4', v_cols, v_cols)
      using v_new_set, (select max(version_no) + 1 from mock_exam_sets where set_group_id = v_src.set_group_id), v_actor, v_src.id;
    select string_agg(quote_ident(column_name), ', ' order by ordinal_position),
           string_agg(case column_name
                        when 'problem_version_id' then 'case when i.problem_id = any ($3) then coalesce(p.published_version_id, i.problem_version_id) else i.problem_version_id end'
                        when 'content_snapshot' then 'case when i.problem_id = any ($3) then null else i.content_snapshot end'
                        else 'i.' || quote_ident(column_name) end, ', ' order by ordinal_position)
      into v_cols, v_cols_i
      from information_schema.columns where table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'mock_exam_set_items' and is_generated = 'NEVER' and column_name not in ('id', 'exam_set_id', 'created_at');
    execute format('insert into mock_exam_set_items (exam_set_id, %s) select $1, %s from mock_exam_set_items i join problems p on p.id = i.problem_id where i.exam_set_id = $2', v_cols, v_cols_i)
      using v_new_set, v_src.id, v_pids;
    if v_src.format = 'mst' and not coalesce((public.mock_exam_validate_mst_set(v_new_set)->>'ready')::boolean, false) then
      raise exception 'New version of % is not ready (4-module blueprint check failed).', v_src.name;
    end if;
    select string_agg(x.problem_id::text || ':' || x.issue, ', ') into v_bad from (select * from public.mock_exam_set_item_issues(v_new_set) where issue is not null limit 5) x;
    if v_bad is not null then raise exception 'New version of % has item issues: %', v_src.name, v_bad; end if;
    perform public.mock_exam_publish_set(v_new_set, v_actor);
    v_done_s := v_done_s + 1;
    raise notice 'set % v% -> v% (%)', v_src.name, v_src.version_no, v_src.version_no + 1, v_new_set;
  end loop;
  raise notice 'DONE problems applied=% skipped=%; sets applied=% skipped=%', v_done_p, v_skip_p, v_done_s, v_skip_s;
end
$audit$;
